{
  "armature": "Avatar_LaPluma",
  "notes": [
    "Joints are Blender XYZ Euler angles (degrees) of a bone in its own rest frame: X across the limb, Y along the bone, Z the third.",
    "The rig faces +Y.  A knee bends about -X (the foot goes back), an elbow about +X (the hand comes forward), a hip bends forward about +X; knees and elbows are hinges -- no turn about Y or Z beyond a little.",
    "A finger's second and third segments copy the first segment's curl (X), as the rig's Copy Rotation constraints do.",
    "A wrist's turn about its bone is shared out along the forearm's twist bones (a share each), so the forearm turns with the hand.",
    "Keypoints are COCO-WholeBody indices (keypoints.py) put on a bone: its head, or `along` its length, plus an `offset` in its frame.",
    "A prop is held in one of its `grips`, the one a shot names: that grip's `hand`, its palm the middle of its two `palm` bones' heads; it closes on the `shaft` (two points in the prop bone's rest frame); the prop's `parts` are told apart by material.  A part's `precision` (and the rest's `rest_precision`) is how hard it is held inside the film's silhouette of it: the film's scythe has the model's blade and hub disc (its ring about the disc's size) but a smaller housing.",
    "A body part is the surface skinned below its bones; a shot's roto masks it under the part's name (roto.py) -- her legs, told apart by the left one's knee pad and strapped thigh; her right arm (it holds the scythe).",
    "A keypoint detector seeing her from behind may swap one pair of limbs and not another: each swap group (inclusive keypoint ranges) is read left-right as it is or swapped.  A group with masked `parts` (left, right) is read by where its sure keypoints fall: a left knee on the right leg's mask is the detector's swap; elsewhere, whichever reading fits.",
    "A limb is fitted by the angles of its `segments` (a keypoint and its parent keypoint): the reference's proportions are not the model's, so only the keypoints without a parent -- face, shoulders, hips -- are pulled onto their places; a hand's root keypoint hangs off its elbow (the wrist's own bone is the same head)."
  ],
